This identifies the material made available under Apache-2.0; it does not add
conditions to, or change, that license. The open-source grant covers permitted
personal and commercial use, modification and redistribution under its terms.

2. Proprietary material excluded from the Apache-2.0 grant

The following directories are not included in the open-source grant above:

- packages/ai/ — see packages/ai/LICENSE.
- packages/core/src/cad/ — see packages/core/src/cad/LICENSE.
- packages/core/src/cam/ — see packages/core/src/cam/LICENSE.

The proprietary terms apply only to material in which the relevant licensor
holds the rights. They also govern copies, modifications and compiled forms of
that material within the scope of those terms. Public source visibility is not
permission to reuse proprietary material. Separate written authorization is
required as stated in each scoped license, subject to mandatory legal rights.

A file containing or incorporating excluded proprietary material does not become
Apache-licensed merely by moving, copying, importing or bundling that material.
Apache-2.0 permission for an open component does not grant permission for a
proprietary component it uses. Building or redistributing the complete application
therefore requires the rights applicable to all included components; the complete
application is not offered as wholly open-source software.

3. Third-party material

Dependencies, vendored material and portions derived from third-party works
retain their applicable licenses and copyright, patent and attribution notices,
including within the proprietary directories. This document does not replace or
restrict rights granted directly by third-party rights holders. See scoped
notices, including packages/core/src/cad/brep/NOTICE,
packages/ai/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and apps/desktop/src-tauri/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
Those notices are scoped attributions, not an exhaustive dependency inventory.

No rights in contributions owned by others are granted beyond the authority of
the person licensing them. Existing valid licenses are not retroactively revoked.
Material excluded from version control, including .reference/, is not made
available under this notice.

4. Marks, user content and separate services

Source-code licensing does not grant a general right to present a fork or service
as an official CADCAMFUN product. Apache-2.0 section 6 and TRADEMARKS.md describe
the applicable trademark boundary without restricting lawful attribution.

Use of the software does not by itself transfer ownership of user projects,
prompts, conversations, models, toolpaths, G-code or manufactured parts. Rights in
third-party inputs, model outputs and copied software remain subject to their
applicable terms. Hosted services, model providers, support and proprietary
application distributions may require separate agreements; this source license
does not promise access to them or change existing agreements.

